<title>SPAIN: Beet sugar content at 17.17 pct for southern Spain.</title>
<headline>Beet sugar content at 17.17 pct for southern Spain.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average sugar content of beets in the Spanish southern crop was 17.17 percent in 1997 for a 1.7 million tonne crop, the National Sugar Beet Association told Reuters on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The southern harvest, which represents roughly one-third of the overall Spanish sugar beet crop, has largely come to a close. The northern harvest begins at the end of September or the start of October.</p>
<p>Average sugar tests for the northern crop should start at about mid-September, the association said.</p>
<p>--Sharman Esarey, Madrid Newsroom, +34 1 585 2167</p>
</text>
